    "revenue_qoq": "FY2026Q4: anchored on the guidance midpoint of $17.0B (Q-1, range $16.49B-$17.51B) versus FY2026Q3 revenue of $13.377B (F-6fa20ae3f8), i.e. 17.0/13.377 - 1 = +27.1% q/q, consistent with the release's stated ~27% sequential increase; supported by Q-3/Q-4 (accelerating Data Center demand, Helios and Venice production ramp). Later quarters (analyst judgment, no guidance): FY2027Q1 +2%, Q2 +6%, Q3 +8%. History shows a seasonally flat Q1 (FY2025Q1 -2.9%, F-d0545641b8 vs D-edca811136; FY2026Q1 -0.2%, F-e8860f2d21 vs D-da671c66c3) followed by strong growth (FY2026Q2 +12.5%, F-0c22036940; Q3 +16.0%, F-6fa20ae3f8). We deliberately grow more slowly than the FY2026Q2-Q4 trend because the Q4 step-up embeds a lumpy rack-scale (Helios) ramp off a much higher base, and export-control risk (Q-6) can interrupt shipments.",
